{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":486436,"name":"Joe LK","username":"Joe_LK","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/joe_lk/{size}/118076_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-08T13:15:23.951Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-486436-feature-request-for-productservice-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-486436-feature-request-for-productservice-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFeature request for product/service\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCloud Agent (GitHub, Slack, Linear,…)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-486436-describe-the-request-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-486436-describe-the-request-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the request\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eREALLY NEED THIS.  I don’t want another listener I have to keep alive. I want Slack to wake my agent the same way Cursor already wakes automations from Slack.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat we have now is a stack of our own pieces. A socket, a webhook routine, wake jobs, and a 5-minute poll as backup. That only works while a process stays running on the agent’s computer. When the computer refreshes, the process dies and mentions sit unseen until someone notices. Last night a teammate \u003cspan class=\"mention\"\u003e@mentioned\u003c/span\u003e our Pepe Silvia bot at 1:32 AM CT and got nothing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe official Slack connector is connected and works for search and sending as me. That is not the same thing. It does not wake the agent when someone mentions the bot in a private work channel.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat I’m asking for:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe same Slack event path Cursor already has, for an agent:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA mention or DM of the agent bot wakes that agent immediately\u003cbr\u003e\nNo socket, webhook routine, wake job, or poll that we have to keep running\u003cbr\u003e\nSurvives a computer refresh\u003cbr\u003e\nReplies as the agent bot, not as my user account\u003cbr\u003e\nWorks in private channels, once the app is invited\u003cbr\u003e\nIf that means connecting Slack as a channel on the agent, and inviting the app into \u003cspan class=\"hashtag-raw\"\u003e#bcp-work\u003c/span\u003e and \u003cspan class=\"hashtag-raw\"\u003e#brc-work\u003c/span\u003e, tell me the exact step and I’ll do it. Right now Pepe’s Slack channel is only a name on file. Mentions never open the chat.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHappy to test one mention after it’s wired and confirm it wakes the agent with nothing else running.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTHANK YOU!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T13:15:32.128Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":5,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":25.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":171036,"topic_slug":"slack-mentions-should-wake-an-agent-the-same-way-cursor-already-does","display_username":"Joe LK","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":133567,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/slack-mentions-should-wake-an-agent-the-same-way-cursor-already-does/171036/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":true},{"id":486626,"name":"Colin","username":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-08T16:34:36.721Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/joe_lk\"\u003e@Joe_LK\u003c/a\u003e I think you’re looking for an Automation like described here!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"quote quote-modified\" data-post=\"5\" data-topic=\"170577\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n    \u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea3.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/48/90452_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"quote-title__text-content\"\u003e\n      \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/subagent-enabled-chatops-in-slack/170577/5\"\u003eSubagent enabled chatops in Slack\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/ideas/feature-requests/5\"\u003e\u003cspan data-category-id=\"5\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #9EB83B; --category-badge-text-color: #000000; --parent-category-badge-color: #ED207B;\" data-parent-category-id=\"22\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category --style-square --has-parent\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"badge-category__name\"\u003eFeature Requests\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003cblockquote\u003e\n    Hey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/bgalvao\"\u003e@bgalvao\u003c/a\u003e, thanks for the suggestion! You can get most of this today without a custom Slack app. \nThe no-code path is an \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/docs/cloud-agent/automations\"\u003eAutomation\u003c/a\u003e with a Slack trigger. Create one automation per “subagent” (for example “ML classifier”), point it at your monorepo, write the instructions your ML engineers want it to follow in the prompt, and set the Slack trigger to your channel with a message filter like /ml-classifier. Leave the trigger open to anyone in the channel, and non-technical teammates can post /ml…\n  \u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eAnd, we are working on an easier way to build bots like this.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T16:34:36.721Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":20.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":171036,"topic_slug":"slack-mentions-should-wake-an-agent-the-same-way-cursor-already-does","display_username":"Colin","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/subagent-enabled-chatops-in-slack/170577/5","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Subagent enabled chatops in Slack","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"Community Support Engineer","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":87436,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/slack-mentions-should-wake-an-agent-the-same-way-cursor-already-does/171036/5","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":486781,"name":"Joe LK","username":"Joe_LK","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/joe_lk/{size}/118076_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-08T19:05:43.117Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThanks, that helps. The Slack trigger on a Cloud Agent is a different job from what I’m after.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStaff talk to a named Grok Bot in Slack, including people who don’t have Cursor. They \u003cspan class=\"mention\"\u003e@mention\u003c/span\u003e that bot in a private work channel. I need that mention to wake that bot and have it reply as itself. No repo, no PR, no slash command, and nothing I have to keep running.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat you described (one automation per agent, \u003ccode\u003e/command\u003c/code\u003e or \u003ccode\u003e@Cursor\u003c/code\u003e, open a PR) doesn’t cover that. The line about named agents you can address directly in Slack is the one we need.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHappy to test a mention in a private channel once that exists.  thank you\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T19:05:43.117Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":0.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":171036,"topic_slug":"slack-mentions-should-wake-an-agent-the-same-way-cursor-already-does","display_username":"Joe LK","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":87436,"username":"Colin","name":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":133567,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/slack-mentions-should-wake-an-agent-the-same-way-cursor-already-does/171036/7","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[486436,486626,486781]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,